  "notes": "Source table on page 45 provides Average Projected Compensation by Age and Years of Service for the Total Plan. The table is split into two rows per age group: counts (top) and average salary (bottom). I transcribed the counts as source_tables[2] to serve as weights for the weighted_avg operation on the '70' target row (which merges '65-69' and '70 & over'). The '40 & over' service bin maps directly to the '40' target. All other bins align exactly. The '70 & over' row in the source contains average salaries; the '65-69' row also contains average salaries. The weighted average is required to merge these two rows into the target '70' bin.",
